Editorial: Paul Brown <brown@erc.msstate.edu> 
 
We still push 7-bit character codes up and down the net. Although 
we may dream of cyberspace and multiuser hypermedia the reality, 
circa February 1993, is ASCII - still the only universal standard. 
Another limitation is a 25Kbyte maximum enforced by some of our 
network exploders.  We intend to overcome these limitations with a 
number of new projects.  Later this year this -e-mail- edition of 
the Forum will contain, in addition to the usual reports and 
announcements, an index of files that will be accessable via a 
public area on the MSU computer network.  We hope also to make use 
of the Gopher services.  Files will be in a variety of formats and 
may include TIFF, EPS and HyperCard as well as other rich-media 
formats. 
 
At this time we plan to include three information areas: 
 
* all items submitted to FineArt Forum and accepted by the editor; 
 
* the FineArt Forum Directory of OnLine Resources which moderator 
  Reed Altemus describes below; and 
 
* the FineArt Forum Online Bibliography - a project I have been 
  dreaming about for several years and am now pleased to see 
  flowering into life.  More below... 
 
