Networker Congress.  I also effected two networked art information 
projects in 1992:  an extension of the"NC92 Telenetlink Congress" 
in July and; " The Computer Is Not Sorry" in November. I'm a  
member of the Electronic Frontier Foundation and the Boston  
Computer Society. In my moderator role, I hope to provide  
assistance to artists in utilizing the connectivity and  
information resources available to them on the datanets. I can 
be contacted at:  raltemus@well.sf.ca.us (not for submissions!) 
 
CALL FOR SUBMISSIONS 
 
   At present we are working on and seek submissions for the 
FineArt Forum "Directory of Online Resources" which we hope will 
be a useful reference resource for online information and  
internetworking for artists, art researchers, art faculty and 
students, and other FineArt Forum subscribers. The directory is 
intended to be a guide to online art resources:  conferencing 
lists, e-journals, databases and search tools that are available 
on the internetworks. What we would like to do with this project  
